35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial reduced readmissions by a fifth, but the shared nursing round failed due to access barriers. We need a program with proven, sustainable impact.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The booking system only tracks fixed slots. Unstructured care vanishes from reports. If the new program lacks rigid appointments, it becomes invisible to us.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The jointly run clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. The outside data agreement took fourteen months. We are building on sand again.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that’s scary! But look, midwifery has slack while therapy is empty. We must balance the load so no team breaks under the new pressure.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The budget shrank, and off-site care earns nothing. We must build on-site to generate revenue. @Benjamin, how do we ensure this program actually pays for itself?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, revenue is secondary to efficacy. The call-back trial proved clinical value, but the nursing round failed due to access barriers. We must design for sustainability, not just profit.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, access barriers are exactly why the shuttle only covers four villages. If patients can’t reach us, the program fails before it starts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Servas, it pays for itself by not collapsing. If we don’t assign a single owner for the rota and budget, we’re just signing a fourteen-month death warrant.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that’s a great point! But @Benjamin, I’m worried about the nine empty nursing posts. If we add more work, the agency costs will skyrocket and break the budget!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, agency costs are a leak we must plug. @Benjamin, a single owner is wise. We must ensure the on-site revenue covers these hidden drains.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, ownership is critical. The call-back trial worked because it was contained. We must avoid the shared round’s access failures by ensuring clear, single-point accountability for patient flow.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, contained is good, but the car park fills before eleven. If we add volume, the physical chokepoint breaks. I need to see the candidates.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the car park is a symptom, not the disease. The disease is ambiguity. If we don’t name the owner now, the budget line vanishes in year two.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I agree! Naming an owner is vital. But please, let’s not forget the midwifery slack. We can balance the new load there, saving the exhausted therapy team from burning out!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, you are right. Ambiguity is the enemy. We must name the owner now, ensuring the on-site revenue sustains the program without hidden deficits.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will vote for the program with the clearest single owner and proven clinical impact. We cannot afford another ambiguous, shared failure.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I will vote for the candidate that fits within our rigid appointment slots and physical limits. If it cannot be booked and housed, it is a failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I will vote for the candidate with a single, named owner and a signed, immediate data agreement. Ambiguity is a death sentence.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I’ll vote for the program that uses midwifery slack to balance the load. We must protect our exhausted therapy team from burning out!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"I will vote for the candidate that generates on-site revenue to cover its true costs. We must build a foundation that sustains itself, not one that quietly collapses.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
